# Review ownership for the files where an unreviewed change is a security event.
#
# WHY (external security research 2026-07-31): two distinct threats converge on
# this file.
#
#   1. **CI/gate tampering.** The workflows hold `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and drive
#      release artefacts, and the gate-configuration files (`.semgrep/`,
#      `deny.toml`, `scripts/gate_enforcement.json`, `supply-chain/`) decide
#      what CI is even allowed to fail on. A PR that quietly weakens a gate is
#      indistinguishable from one that fixes it unless a human who owns the
#      gate reads it.
#
#   2. **AI-instruction-file poisoning.** `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/`
#      and `.cursorrules` are executed-as-instructions by every coding agent
#      that touches this repo. The May-2026 TrapDoor campaign shipped poisoned
#      `CLAUDE.md`/`.cursorrules` files through ordinary pull requests to major
#      projects: the payload is not code, so it survives code review that only
#      looks at diffs of `.rs`/`.sol`. Treat a diff to these files as a change
#      to the build system, because for an agent it is one.
#
# LIMITATION, stated so nobody over-reads this file: CODEOWNERS is ADVISORY
# until "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in branch-protection
# settings, which needs repo-admin. Landed here so the mapping is reviewed and
# in place; flipping the branch-protection switch is tracked separately.
#
# Syntax note: last matching pattern wins, so keep the broad default first.

